{"title":"2015 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 24","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(similar_to_3)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (similar to 3)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5_(Similar_to_Solution_1)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5 (Similar to Solution 1)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Solution_7(Similar_to_3,4)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 7(Similar to 3,4)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Aaron the ant walks on the coordinate plane according to the following rules. He starts at the origin <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/7/6b7c84b8d338464090337f21083f0b4b1e7f659f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p_0=(0,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"80\" height=\"18\" /> facing to the east and walks one unit, arriving at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/d/8ad253e7e0042f767f5b3f1bf58c96c3c13314c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p_1=(1,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"80\" height=\"18\" />. For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/f/7afd5ca011531278306bbde19218bfbd02dc37d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=1,2,3,\\dots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"106\" height=\"16\" />, right after arriving at the point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/1/df151678062aa7e93180c689cab0c21a2563e351.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"18\" height=\"11\" />, if Aaron can turn <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/e/22ec0d2e4202839322d26a23dcb13f79821df5d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$90^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"28\" height=\"15\" /> left and walk one unit to an unvisited point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/5/7b50273c24a79c46b1bb09917df4634e75cc60fc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p_{n+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"33\" height=\"12\" />, he does that. Otherwise, he walks one unit straight ahead to reach <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/5/7b50273c24a79c46b1bb09917df4634e75cc60fc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p_{n+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"33\" height=\"12\" />. Thus the sequence of points continues <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/7/ef7b97b3a7ea832f09fb54815b9c4edc5feffaac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p_2=(1,1), p_3=(0,1), p_4=(-1,1), p_5=(-1,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"377\" height=\"18\" />, and so on in a counterclockwise spiral pattern. What is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/0/b406af0fd387a52b5e24c27953f036e3c0e6caa3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p_{2015}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"35\" height=\"11\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/0/880ee7fe403e392728fbe9d8943998d72dead32e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } (-22,-13)\\qquad\\textbf{(B) } (-13,-22)\\qquad\\textbf{(C) } (-13,22)\\qquad\\textbf{(D) } (13,-22)\\qquad\\textbf{(E) } (22,-13)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"698\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/c/d9ce7e6077089fc709926ba1cefe4dc73726bc8d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] draw( (0,0)--(1,0)--(1,1)--(-1,1)--(-1,-1)--(1,-1)--(2,-1)--(2,2)--(-2,2)--(-2,-2)--(3,-2)--(3,3) ); label(&quot;$p_1$&quot;, (1,0), SE); label(&quot;$p_4$&quot;, (-1,1), NW); label(&quot;$p_9$&quot;, (2,-1), SE); label(&quot;$p_{16}$&quot;, (-2,2), NW); label(&quot;$p_{25}$&quot;, (3,-2), SE);  draw( (0,4)--(0,-4) ); label(&quot;$y$&quot;, (0,4), NW); draw( (-4,0)--(4,0) ); label(&quot;$x$&quot;, (-4,0), NW);  [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"252\" /> \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The first thing we would do is track Aaron's footsteps:\n</p><p>He starts by taking <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> step East and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> step North, ending at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/7/ae7a465ffe5255961382f5777569608be052b783.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1,1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" /> after <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> steps and about to head West.\n</p><p>Then he takes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> steps West and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> steps South, ending at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/a/c0ad82b10660edf6340c332e04c70ee71a951300.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(-1,-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"60\" height=\"18\" />) after <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/1/ee1a83cfd5c8598dc1fc9fc8ed98d55bebce3ac5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2+4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"40\" height=\"13\" /> steps, and about to head East.\n</p><p>Then he takes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> steps East and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> steps North, ending at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/b/b2b596a120dcf60e33c7bfe19003bb1675bf37a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2,2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" /> after <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/98662d9ab8322708539f218c814d9d0213ad3788.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2+4+6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"71\" height=\"14\" /> steps, and about to head West.\n</p><p>Then he takes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> steps West and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> steps South, ending at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/f/e0f362b2b408e022f4ecbaed09d2f120a4bfd97e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(-2,-2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"71\" height=\"20\" /> after <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/e/abef7b7aa79e2fea135c3be34d5e7f1c031b752e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2+4+6+8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"105\" height=\"15\" /> steps, and about to head East.\n</p><p>From this pattern, we can notice that for any integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/2/172e6dadffd9800e796f3f96a1e24ce2a1840f3a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k \\ge 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" /> he's at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/9/d197c92e7992026dc9444b52e577ec8dba9c9cfc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(-k, -k)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"69\" height=\"18\" /> after <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/6/a56433db12ceceddc68c6a27859d68ad3dc92596.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 + 4 + 6 + ... + 4k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"152\" height=\"16\" /> steps, and about to head East.  There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/e/b8ea7ee8a282949fd853a01537ec7a2b55e56f75.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2k$\" width=\"18\" height=\"12\" /> terms in the sum, with an average value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/8/2280d83755a0268f07dbb1deb8596909972442f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2 + 4k)/2 = 2k + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"156\" height=\"18\" />, so:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/e/abe2c1579bcfaa3d307e00f78ea511e026a2b9d7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2 + 4 + 6 + ... + 4k = 2k(2k + 1)\\]\" width=\"256\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>If we substitute <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/d/a0dbf4bdff8dce668c17676669a414d2c82c85b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = 22$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"54\" height=\"14\" /> into the equation:  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/f/bdf7a12d58f42bbd0913022e2354efe78e88f05c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$44(45) = 1980 &lt; 2015$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"171\" height=\"18\" />.  So he has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/7/8c7f6c79f2148f0cec592c9517b40ee1b82ef22e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$35$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> moves to go.  This makes him end up at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/e/fdec1f477426c02c3adec542fc8a65ef0382a542.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(-22+35,-22) = (13,-22) \\implies \\boxed{\\textbf{(D)} (13, -22)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"387\" height=\"29\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We are given that Aaron starts at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/b/c4b86f54134d69cad8793688a431aa907aaf2698.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0, 0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" />, and we note that his net steps follow the pattern of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/7/1178af8fcc5f3f3acb9f151f7dcc2c4eefe88fd9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"22\" height=\"13\" /> in the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />-direction, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/7/1178af8fcc5f3f3acb9f151f7dcc2c4eefe88fd9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"22\" height=\"13\" /> in the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />-direction, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/a/62a76677add1d246708c86edfc7c4b8a40184914.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" /> in the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />-direction, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/a/62a76677add1d246708c86edfc7c4b8a40184914.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" /> in the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />-direction, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/6/a26d26d140649aac91fff6adf22f9c795c935801.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$+3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" /> in the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />-direction, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/6/a26d26d140649aac91fff6adf22f9c795c935801.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$+3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" /> in the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />-direction, and so on, where we add odd and subtract even.\n</p><p>We want <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/a/4ca5ef1f2e8b3535965b3bded67b3c5f096fdeed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 + 4 + 6 + 8 + ... + 2n = 2015$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"242\" height=\"14\" />, but it does not work out cleanly. Instead, we get that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/c/17cbb19dc62f4d1fc3bc66dd53bad943d9a38be7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 + 4 + 6 + ... + 2(44) = 1980$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"232\" height=\"18\" />, which means that there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/7/8c7f6c79f2148f0cec592c9517b40ee1b82ef22e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$35$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> extra steps past adding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/3/e4365fd6613b120e5fac37829e0e81dc7313a455.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-44$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"32\" height=\"12\" /> in the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />-direction (and the final number we add in the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />-direction is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/3/e4365fd6613b120e5fac37829e0e81dc7313a455.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-44$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"32\" height=\"12\" />).\n</p><p>So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/f/66f1e35e5d6313625c50a19ca4a161609992e834.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p_{2015} = (0+1-2+3-4+5...-44+35, 0+1-2+3-4+5...-44)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"565\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>We can group <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/d/6ad67b2aa16baabccc9e934d361debfce4ca2b18.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1-2+3-4+5...-44$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"189\" height=\"14\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/4/2b4244dafe0b5350b3fd4711e6912b31e736455a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1-2)+(3-4)+(5-6)+...+(43-44) = -22$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"396\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/5/8955fce29b10558d76bddc5a725c4816229d7c20.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p_{2015} = \\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\; (13, -22)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"180\" height=\"29\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Looking at his steps, we see that he walks in a spiral shape. At the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />th step, he is on the bottom right corner of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/5/7b5343f2d9e22816e8de24262565ff2937695b2c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3\\times 3$\" width=\"40\" height=\"12\" /> square centered on the origin. On the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/9/e290f2cba0ba0e11c0b91630da15a408da2fcf1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />th step, he is on the bottom right corner of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/7/ef7fe7592026585cc36e4d7c6036f19fd8afdc29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5\\times 5$\" width=\"40\" height=\"12\" /> square centered at the origin. It seems that the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/2/bd26f70658dc1780d619834c085d117b1b70f790.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p_{n^2-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"41\" height=\"11\" /> is the bottom right corner of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/f/93f761f7fc79f2bec21a2f31c896840d6f36cdc0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\times n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> square. This makes sense since, after <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/b/5cb69df5577de55ff087bfc5fd090a6ea28c5c31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^2-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"48\" height=\"15\" />, he has been on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/0/6006bba637eef443381fbaff768fa62d9ff41e62.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"17\" /> dots, including the point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/e/d4e8cf09c5ced63a38ed87c9a03dd9aacf7e490a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"16\" height=\"11\" />. Also, this is only for odd <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, because starting with the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/8/8a8df7312744a199daa5c8008af5b9b4798bfd64.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1\\times 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"39\" height=\"12\" /> square, we can only add one extra set of dots to each side, so we cannot get even <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/e/c5efab1fe69d482f224850979c04161d3fd44fd5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$45^2=2025$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"85\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/2/a028948e80563a797a6ab100e88ac90ae20fbc48.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p_{2024}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"13\" /> is the bottom right corner of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/b/c0bb7666bd6e7d779f67760ff823345308f09d0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$45\\times 45$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" /> square. This point is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/2/f028a936c2d24b386c73a3fab0d820931d90291d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{45-1}{2}=22$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"95\" height=\"37\" /> over to the right, and therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/1/1d111a5e00ee5ea6700bb629994dc629874c505b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$22$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> down, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/1/9a1b44968f8c07eba7287137a0a8d90b9d37460d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p_{2024}=(22, -22)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"132\" height=\"18\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/2/a028948e80563a797a6ab100e88ac90ae20fbc48.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p_{2024}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> ahead of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/0/b406af0fd387a52b5e24c27953f036e3c0e6caa3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p_{2015}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"35\" height=\"11\" />, we go back <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> spaces to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/9/179391096d1f0e80c165353fabba954f26bcd1d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\; (13, -22)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"119\" height=\"29\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28similar_to_3.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(similar_to_3)\">Solution 4 (similar to 3)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (similar to 3)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We call <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/e/d4e8cf09c5ced63a38ed87c9a03dd9aacf7e490a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"16\" height=\"11\" /> the first point, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/1/e01486dcc7cb25518b89692706b17389dc67c92b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"15\" height=\"11\" /> the second, and so on. As in Solution 3, we see that he walks in a counterclockwise spiral. We see that his path is traced out by a series of squares with odd-length sides that contain each other. At step <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5bdc836573d490dbb4fec6ff77fcd6cf176244.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3^2=9,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"57\" height=\"20\" /> he is at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/0/350caf4c4803973cd5992382cc5cac99f9bf45f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1,-1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"52\" height=\"18\" />; at step <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/3/ee3d153d9d7ac4a17d74881a86441f9792a81208.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5^2=25,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"66\" height=\"20\" /> he is at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/1/211f55c01222ffbccc389f0d79159ad07ad77d48.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2,-2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"52\" height=\"18\" />; and so on. We see that at step <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/0/6006bba637eef443381fbaff768fa62d9ff41e62.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"17\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is an odd number, he is at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/2/fb20edaff3c41177d4e9746189ec799f1c264a1e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x,-x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"55\" height=\"18\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/e/5ae703da77951a84801bee16740f706c5256bde1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=\\dfrac{n-1}2.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"88\" height=\"38\" /> The closest <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/0/6006bba637eef443381fbaff768fa62d9ff41e62.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"17\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/7/4b781fdf1cd172b567be38e2ffa6f20f0b8390c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2016$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" /> (we want <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/8/5d80917f7407309f351328c1981e3eec1cd7ad90.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p_{2015},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" /> which is the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/7/4b781fdf1cd172b567be38e2ffa6f20f0b8390c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2016$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" />th step) is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/0/3f0a658ed3e96737d381d61ce9c48af0329f3d3a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$45^2=2025,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"93\" height=\"20\" /> so we let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/6/df652b35deadf2d97198b800694d8568a413d879.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=45.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> On the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/e/c5efab1fe69d482f224850979c04161d3fd44fd5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$45^2=2025$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"85\" height=\"15\" />th step, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/8/ef808b453aa832d83b053233cdb52cfe347d4917.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=\\dfrac{45-1}2=22,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"137\" height=\"38\" /> so he is at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/7/d27186abbbf4aaff3fb0257cee22436b70739aaf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(22,-22).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"80\" height=\"20\" /> We see that he approached <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/6/6a63bd9f50db1825eb490f541836e9907fdd578e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(22,-22)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"75\" height=\"20\" /> from the left, so backtrack <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/0/01047f9e58310de881b9dc40c25194d76f82f08c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2025-2016=9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"130\" height=\"15\" /> steps to the left (i.e. subtracting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> from the x-coordinate). Thus, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/3/ef3ec7ded68aa4c00bcbc9ecce39df750d2a6898.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(22-9,-22)=\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}~(13,-22).}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"254\" height=\"32\" /> \n~Technodoggo\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_5_.28Similar_to_Solution_1.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5_(Similar_to_Solution_1)\">Solution 5 (Similar to Solution 1)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5 (Similar to Solution 1)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The first thing is to see the amount of footsteps at points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/4/4347d1b0f4733a8f31115cbee1cdceb245ab4645.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(k,k)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"40\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>We see that at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/7/ae7a465ffe5255961382f5777569608be052b783.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1,1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" /> he has taken 2 footsteps.\n</p><p>To get to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/b/b2b596a120dcf60e33c7bfe19003bb1675bf37a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2,2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, Aaron takes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> steps West, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> steps South, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> steps East, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> steps North.\n</p><p>We can think about this in the following way. For Aaron to get from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/4/4347d1b0f4733a8f31115cbee1cdceb245ab4645.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(k,k)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"40\" height=\"18\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/8/4f87623d2289eec91c084d5375f187ddddd031f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(k+1,k+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"107\" height=\"20\" />, he takes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/b/3fb02fb9643884f8b1492e1fdcde12f213d721fe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2k+2k+(2k+1)+(2k+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"236\" height=\"20\" /> steps = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/5/e751750411e49360f6f9b8242680fa1404dc3d99.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8k+2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"52\" height=\"16\" /> steps\n</p><p>We can find the total steps taken to get to a point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/8/4f87623d2289eec91c084d5375f187ddddd031f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(k+1,k+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"107\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/8/eb8410e77fbc75424837cec3c8087c3c93ba05ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2+10+18... +8k+2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"180\" height=\"16\" /> = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/9/4f93f2b583a32d728a5d4576f485bb577f34bdda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(4k+2)(k+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"115\" height=\"20\" />) works as a formula\n</p><p>We find that to get to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/e/1ce5caa7f20a8078cce83b8ec8c08610d19c589c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(22,22)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"57\" height=\"18\" /> this is 2+10+18...+ (4(21)+2)(21)= 1892. We then simply go <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/d/40d924a5d0ade21a3824a7f0343f8beae70ef96e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$88$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> steps to get to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/a/eba0f36deee0b710bb85fd338ea1a62582e4b8b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(-22,-22)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"89\" height=\"20\" /> \n</p><p>and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/7/8c7f6c79f2148f0cec592c9517b40ee1b82ef22e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$35$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> more to get to the 2015th step at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/d/99dc0d0e18f6502cea406d6b691f1058a604e125.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(13,-22)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"75\" height=\"20\" /> or answer D\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6\">Solution 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If we graph <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/1/df151678062aa7e93180c689cab0c21a2563e351.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"18\" height=\"11\" /> for a few values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, we begin to see a particular pattern for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/1/df151678062aa7e93180c689cab0c21a2563e351.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"18\" height=\"11\" /> when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is a perfect square. For example, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/7/6b7c84b8d338464090337f21083f0b4b1e7f659f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p_0=(0,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"80\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/6/e6672684b94482ec83667870640dd8edb09d63f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p_4=(-1,1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"97\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/7/8a71762a705ca3e51b2e75636735a80cd57e8992.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p_{16}=(-2, 2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"104\" height=\"20\" />, and so on. Similarly, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/d/8ad253e7e0042f767f5b3f1bf58c96c3c13314c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p_1=(1,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"80\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/a/41aeac78520ff09f815b2306cc6da3f3271943cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p_9=(2,-1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"97\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/d/22da6b5905e53f29c6a584b0c8fb8e59096d6e06.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p_{25}=(3,-2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"104\" height=\"20\" />, and so on. Using this, we can generate a pattern for even and odd squares: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/b/04bf3f0e5defcf1a749542203324a26800487de6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[p_{(2n)^2}=(-n, n)\\]\" width=\"123\" height=\"19\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/4/fa44abd866a5d2e32dd3a767dea4a31131de3208.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[p_{(2n+1)^2}=(n+1,-n)\\]\" width=\"171\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p>We notice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/0/b406af0fd387a52b5e24c27953f036e3c0e6caa3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p_{2015}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"35\" height=\"11\" /> is quite close to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/9/049ca537d9c7e22ccf8ab50ea8c39178aadd4e70.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p_{2025}=p_{45^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"92\" height=\"13\" />. By the same pattern for odd squares, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/9/4f90d687d4d2412cb76d8f707f4a33a37b6d921e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p_{2025}=(23,-22)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"135\" height=\"20\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/0/b406af0fd387a52b5e24c27953f036e3c0e6caa3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p_{2015}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"35\" height=\"11\" /> is just <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> units to the left of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/c/e2cc8b7456f4012688a04277a185a77bb5cce035.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p_{2025}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"13\" />. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/c/94c462a5ae4f9844f444294fac5da64fddff3f55.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p_{2015}=\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }(13,-22)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"182\" height=\"32\" />.\n</p><p>~<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php/User:Sid2012\">sid2012</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_7.28Similar_to_3.2C4.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_7(Similar_to_3,4)\">Solution 7(Similar to 3,4)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 7(Similar to 3,4)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Consider <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/0/4508393135451dc6c41b01f36072dd16674586bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"17\" height=\"11\" />. Notice that for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> that are odd squares, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/0/4508393135451dc6c41b01f36072dd16674586bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"17\" height=\"11\" /> is in the fourth quadrant, while <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> that are even squares are located in the second quadrant. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/c/e2cc8b7456f4012688a04277a185a77bb5cce035.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p_{2025}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"13\" /> is in the fourth quadrant. Furthermore, by observation the value of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> coordinate of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/e/b5e24a94b7aabff2c1ecf896e7e55e6633137aaf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p_{k}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"17\" height=\"11\" />, for odd perfect square <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />, is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/2/e925540a36b7f5a6981f17ac90ed5233fdbdc361.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$- \\frac{ \\sqrt{k} -1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"76\" height=\"44\" />; likewise, the absolute value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> coordinate is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/b/37b1653552dada49913ce375f9a8abe3c3e65b21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{ \\sqrt{k} +1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"62\" height=\"44\" />. Thus, the coordinates of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/c/e2cc8b7456f4012688a04277a185a77bb5cce035.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p_{2025}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"13\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/4/3b4bb0e736d6946ec69feab81dd7bfc715da1768.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(23,-22)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"75\" height=\"20\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/0/b406af0fd387a52b5e24c27953f036e3c0e6caa3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p_{2015}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"35\" height=\"11\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> steps backward relative to Aaron the ant's movement, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/0/000ff825f1eefc5f10272f2763aea8e6ac2a9883.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p_{2015} = (13,-22)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"135\" height=\"20\" />, and we choose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/a/2ca5891135ba5bf0cea3e0a0e45d2bbdd9cad58f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{ (D) }$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"43\" height=\"32\" />. \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B\" title=\"2015 AMC 10B\">2015 AMC 10B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2015 AMC 10B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2015 AMC 10B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2015 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 23\">Problem 23</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_25\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2015 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 25\">Problem 25</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2015 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2015 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2015 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2015 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2015 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2015 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2015 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2015 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2015 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2015 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2015 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2015 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2015 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2015 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2015 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2015 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2015 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2015 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2015 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2015 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2015 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2015 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2015 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_25\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2015 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_10_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 10 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 10 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017003605\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.067 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.085 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 923/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2324/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 158/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 29315/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.927      1 -total\n 61.36%    7.932      1 Template:AMC10_box\n 37.63%    4.865      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:14087:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017003605 and revision id 264010. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}